            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cavarsela — \"to come through all right, to get by\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "È stato un brutto incidente, ma ce la siamo cavata. It was a bad accident, but we came through it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An idiom: me la cavo, se l'è cavata. Also ‘to manage’: me la cavo con l'inglese."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cavarsela is built on cavare \"to dig out, to pull out\", which is inherited from Latin cavāre \"to hollow out\" (Lewis & Short): to pull oneself out of trouble."
            }
          ]
        },
